  "content": {
    "id": "p17-q9-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "The length of a rectangular lawn is 3 m shorter than twice the width. There is a path around the lawn 0.75 m wide. Let the width of the lawn be $x$ metres.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p17-q9-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Express the length of the lawn in terms of $x$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(2x-3)\\text{ m}$",
          "worked": "$$L=2x-3\\text{ m}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q9-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Express the area of the lawn in terms of $x$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x(2x-3)\\text{ m}^2$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}A_{\\text{lawn}}&=x(2x-3)\\\\A_{\\text{lawn}}&=(2x^2-3x)\\text{ m}^2.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 14
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q9-c",
        "type": "group",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p17-q9-c-i",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "i",
            "prompt": {
              "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
              "version": 1,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p17-q9-c-i-given",
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "fontSize": null,
                  "align": "left",
                  "spaceBefore": 0,
                  "spaceAfter": 2,
                  "lineHeight": 1.4,
                  "indent": 0,
                  "inlines": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Show that the area ",
                      "marks": []
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "math",
                      "latex": "A\\text{ m}^2",
                      "display": false
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " of the path in terms of ",
                      "marks": []
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "math",
                      "latex": "x",
                      "display": false
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " is ",
                      "marks": []
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "math",
                      "latex": "A=\\frac{9(2x-1)}{4}",
                      "display": false
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": ".",
                      "marks": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$A=\\dfrac{9(2x-1)}4\\text{ m}^2$.\n\nSubtract the lawn area from the area of the outer rectangle.",
              "worked": "The outer rectangle has width $x+1.5$ m and length $(2x-3)+1.5=2x-1.5$ m.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=(x+1.5)(2x-1.5)-x(2x-3)\\\\A&=2x^2+1.5x-2.25-2x^2+3x\\\\A&=4.5x-2.25\\\\A&=\\frac{9(2x-1)}4\\text{ m}^2.\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 42
          },
          {
            "id": "p17-q9-c-ii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "ii",
            "prompt": "If the area of the path is $20.25\\text{ m}^2$, find $x$.",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$x=5$",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{9(2x-1)}4&=20.25\\\\9(2x-1)&=81\\\\2x-1&=9\\\\2x&=10\\\\x&=5.\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 32
          },
          {
            "id": "p17-q9-c-iii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "iii",
            "prompt": "Find the area of the lawn using the value of $x$ obtained in part ii.",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$35\\text{ m}^2$",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}A_{\\text{lawn}}&=x(2x-3)\\\\A_{\\text{lawn}}&=5(2\\times5-3)\\\\A_{\\text{lawn}}&=35\\text{ m}^2.\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 20
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q9-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "If the area of the lawn is $90\\text{ m}^2$, find the corresponding value of $x$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\dfrac{15}{2}=7.5$.\n\nFactorise the area equation and reject the negative width.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x(2x-3)&=90\\\\2x^2-3x-90&=0\\\\(2x-15)(x+6)&=0.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThus $x=\\dfrac{15}{2}$ or $x=-6$. A width must be positive, so $x=\\dfrac{15}{2}=7.5$.\n\nCheck: $7.5(2\\times7.5-3)=7.5\\times12=90\\text{ m}^2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      }
    ]
  },
